<title>USA: MetroNet Communications to sell $200 mln 144a debt.</title>
<headline>MetroNet Communications to sell $200 mln 144a debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>MetroNet Communications Corp, a Canadian local telephone services provider, was expected to sell $200 million in U.S. junk bonds in the next few weeks via a Salomon Brothers syndicate, according to market sources.</p>
<p>The deal would be comprised of 10-year debt and structured with a two- to three-year interest reserve, one source said.</p>
<p>MetroNet and Salomon Brothers declined comment.</p>
<p>MetroNet is based in Calgary, Alberta, Canada.</p>
<p>(( -- Al Yoon, 212-859-1672 ))</p>
